WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.415 --> 00:00:18.753
A shift starts when you open the register. Go to Sales, POS Terminal.

2
00:00:18.853 --> 00:00:24.328
The register bar at the top shows when the shift opened and has the two cash buttons.

3
00:00:24.428 --> 00:00:28.258
Select Cash in/out to record money added to the drawer.

4
00:00:28.359 --> 00:00:33.616
Cash in is selected. Enter the amount, then choose a reason such as Float top-up.

5
00:00:33.716 --> 00:00:39.254
Add a note if you like and select Save. The movement is on this shift's report.

6
00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:44.501
Use Cash in/out again, this time for money leaving the drawer. Choose Cash out.

7
00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:51.557
Enter the amount and a reason such as Safe drop. You cannot take out more than the drawer should hold.

8
00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:54.878
At the end of the day select Close Register.

9
00:00:54.978 --> 00:01:01.609
Count the cash in the drawer and type the Counted cash. Here the count is a little short, so a note helps.

10
00:01:01.709 --> 00:01:05.756
Select Close Register. The shift ends and its report opens.

11
00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:12.431
The report compares the cash you counted with the cash the drawer should hold. The Difference is the gap.

12
00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:19.218
Scroll down for the cash movements you just made. Payments and sales made in the shift are listed here too.

13
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:26.275
Sales, Shifts lists every shift, with its sales total, expected cash, counted cash and difference.

14
00:01:26.375 --> 00:01:31.149
Tick Only shifts with a difference to find drawers that did not balance.
